    "number": 106,
    "summary": "1–3, Warren A. Cowdery is called as a local presiding officer; 4–5, The Second Coming will not overtake the children of light as a thief; 6–8, Great blessings follow faithful service in the Church.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [
      {
        "type": "introduction",
        "text": "Revelation given through Joseph Smith the Prophet, at Kirtland, Ohio, November 25, 1834. This revelation is directed to Warren A. Cowdery, an older brother of Oliver Cowdery."
      }
    ],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "It is my will that my servant Warren A. Cowdery should be appointed and ordained a presiding high priest over my church, in the land of Freedom and the regions round about;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 143,
            "text": "IE the city of Freedom, New York, and environs."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Doctrine and Covenants 106:1",
        "book": "Doctrine and Covenants",
        "chapter": 106,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And should preach my everlasting gospel, and lift up his voice and warn the people, not only in his own place, but in the adjoining counties;",
        "footNotes": [
